From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 06:46:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 47/47] Android: no fused multiply-add in VU0 macro mode and
 the CPU GS

NDK clang contracts acc + a*b into one fused multiply-add by default
(-ffp-contract=on): Kernel/Stubs/VU.cpp (the sceVu0* macro-mode library
the game calls) had 458 fmadd/fmla-class instructions in the Android
object, gs/gs_cpu_backend.cpp 36. The PS2, PCSX2 and our Windows (MSVC)
build round the multiply and the add separately, so Android results
differed in the last bits. Both files now include ps2_no_fp_contract.h
first: the same pragmas as ps2_vu1_detail.h (patch 0045) turn
contraction off for the translation unit. Android objects: 0 fused ops
in both (llvm-objdump). Game units are untouched (runtime .cpp only).

Test (ps2x, PS2VU0Math): sceVu0InnerProduct of (1,0,0,1+2^-12) and
(-1,0,0,1+2^-12) is 0x3A000000 (product rounded to 1+2^-11, then -1);
fused into the running sum, fma(x3, y3, -1) gives 0x3A000400. The same
expression built with g++ -O2 -mfma -ffp-contract=fast gives 0x3A000400,
with contraction off 0x3A000000.
---
 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/VU.cpp   |  1 +
 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_cpu_backend.cpp |  1 +
 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_no_fp_contract.h  | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 ps2xTest/src/ps2_vu_tests.cpp             | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 37 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_no_fp_contract.h

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/VU.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/VU.cpp
index b7840d4..99f0900 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/VU.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/VU.cpp
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+#include "../../ps2_no_fp_contract.h" // no fused multiply-add: VU0 macro mode rounds a*b, then +
 #include "Common.h"
 #include "VU.h"
 
diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_cpu_backend.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_cpu_backend.cpp
index f0ad507..322360a 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_cpu_backend.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_cpu_backend.cpp
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+#include "../ps2_no_fp_contract.h" // no fused multiply-add, as Windows/PCSX2 round
 #include "runtime/gs/gs_cpu_backend.h"
 #include "runtime/gs/ps2_gs_common.h"
 #include "runtime/gs/ps2_gs_psmct16.h"
diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_no_fp_contract.h b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_no_fp_contract.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6b04449
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_no_fp_contract.h
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+#ifndef PS2_NO_FP_CONTRACT_H
+#define PS2_NO_FP_CONTRACT_H
+
+// Floating-point contraction off for the rest of the translation unit. The PS2 (VU0 macro mode, the GS
+// rasteriser's interpolation as PCSX2 and our Windows build compute it) rounds every multiply and every add
+// separately; MSVC x64 never fuses them. NDK clang (-ffp-contract=on by default) and GCC (-ffp-contract=fast)
+// turn `acc + a * b` into one fused multiply-add on arm64 (or with FMA), one rounding instead of two, and the
+// results differ from Windows in the last bits. Include first, before any code (ps2_vu1_detail.h does the same
+// for the VU1 files, patch 0045).
+#if defined(__clang__)
+#pragma STDC FP_CONTRACT OFF
+#elif defined(_MSC_VER)
+#pragma fp_contract(off)
+#elif defined(__GNUC__)
+#pragma GCC optimize("fp-contract=off")
+#endif
+
+#endif
diff --git a/ps2xTest/src/ps2_vu_tests.cpp b/ps2xTest/src/ps2_vu_tests.cpp
index b96befe..e543717 100644
--- a/ps2xTest/src/ps2_vu_tests.cpp
